            </TextBlock>
            <!-- ID, Key, and Name Fields -->
            <TextBlock Text="Item ID, Key, and Name" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Every item has three fundamental identifier fields:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="ID"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A read-only unique identifier auto-generated when the item is created (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="myproject_item_0001"/><Run Text="). The ID is used internally to link items to spawns, loot tables, shops, and quests. It cannot be changed after creation to preserve referential integrity."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Key"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The primary display name of the item (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Iron Sword"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Health Potion"/><Run Text="). This is what players see in-game and what appears in spawn dropdowns, shop lists, and loot tables. The Key must be unique across all items &#8212; the editor validates this and shows an error if you enter a duplicate Key."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Name"/><Run Text=" &#8212; An optional display name that can differ from the Key. When set, the Name field overrides the Key for in-game display purposes. This is useful for items that have a short Key for reference but a longer, more descriptive Name for players (e.g., Key = "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="rusty_sword"/><Run Text=", Name = "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Rusty Iron Sword of the Forgotten Guard"/><Run Text=")."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Changing the Key or Name marks the project as dirty. If you change the Key to a value already used by another item, a validation message appears immediately, and the change is not committed until the conflict is resolved."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Type and Category -->
            <TextBlock Text="Item Type and Category" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Two dropdown fields classify how the item behaves in the game world:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Type"/><Run Text=" &#8212; Determines the item's base behavior. Available types include: "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Weapon"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Armor"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Consumable"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Quest"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Key"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Container"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Currency"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Readable"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Light"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Tool"/><Run Text=", and "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Object"/><Run Text=" (generic). The Type influences how the item is exported to Evennia and which rules apply to it in-game."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Category"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A secondary classification used for organization and loot filtering. Categories are user-definable and help group items by theme or purpose (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Weapons"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Potions"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Quest Items"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Valuables"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Keys"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Misc"/><Run Text=")."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Changing Type or Category marks the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>
            <!-- Description and Notes -->
            <TextBlock Text="Description and Notes" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Two multi-line text fields let you provide documentation and narrative detail for each item:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Description"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The flavor text shown to players when they examine the item in-game (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="A well-worn iron blade, its edge still sharp despite years of neglect."/><Run Text="). This field supports freeform text and is exported as the item's Evennia description."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Notes"/><Run Text=" &#8212; Designer-only notes that are "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="not exported"/><Run Text=" to Evennia. Use this field for internal documentation, reminders, design rationale, or implementation todos. Notes are visible only within The Forge."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Both fields support multi-line text. Editing either field marks the project as dirty. Text changes support undo/redo with coalescing, so only the before/after values are stored."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Requirements -->
            <TextBlock Text="Requirements" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Requirements define the conditions a player must meet to equip or use the item:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Level"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The minimum character level required. Leave blank or set to 0 for no level requirement."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Strength"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Dexterity"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Intelligence"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Wisdom"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Constitution"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Charisma"/><Run Text=" &#8212; Numeric stat requirements. Each field accepts an integer value; leave blank or 0 for no requirement."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Skill"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A skill name or identifier required to use the item (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Lockpicking"/><Run Text=" for a lockpick, "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Alchemy"/><Run Text=" for a potion kit)."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Skill Level"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The minimum level of the required skill."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Stat requirement fields are numeric-only. Non-numeric input is rejected. Changing any requirement field marks the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>
            <!-- Modifiers -->
            <TextBlock Text="Modifiers" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Modifiers define how the item affects a character's stats when equipped or used. Each modifier entry has three components:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Stat"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The stat being modified (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Attack"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Defense"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="HP"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="MP"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Speed"/><Run Text=", or any custom stat defined in your game)."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Value"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The numeric amount (positive for bonuses, negative for penalties). For example, a sword might have Attack +5, while cursed armor might have Speed -2."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Type"/><Run Text=" &#8212; How the modifier is applied: "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Flat"/><Run Text=" (adds/subtracts directly) or "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Percent"/><Run Text=" (multiplies the base stat by a percentage)."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Use the "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Add Modifier"/><Run Text=" button to create a new modifier row. Use the "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Remove"/><Run Text=" button (X) on each row to delete that modifier."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Modifier changes (add, remove, edit) are all "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="undoable"/><Run Text=" and mark the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Effects -->
            <TextBlock Text="Effects" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Effects define special behaviors that trigger when the item is used, equipped, or consumed. Like modifiers, each effect entry has several fields:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Effect Type"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The kind of effect: "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Heal"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Damage"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Buff"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Debuff"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Teleport"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Summon"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Status"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Script"/><Run Text=", or "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Custom"/><Run Text="."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Target"/><Run Text=" &#8212; Who or what the effect applies to: "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Self"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Target"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Area"/><Run Text=", or "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Room"/><Run Text="."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Value"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The numeric magnitude of the effect (e.g., heal amount, damage dealt, buff strength)."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Duration"/><Run Text=" &#8212; How long the effect lasts in seconds. 0 means instantaneous; a positive number creates a temporary effect."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Script"/><Run Text=" &#8212; For Script and Custom types, a reference to a Python script or function name (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="world.scripts.poison_effect"/><Run Text=")."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Use the "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Add Effect"/><Run Text=" button to add a new effect row. Remove individual effects with the X button on each row."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Effect changes are "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="undoable"/><Run Text=" and mark the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>
            <!-- Sources -->
            <TextBlock Text="Sources" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Sources define where and how the item can be obtained in the game world. This information is used by the Evennia export to generate acquisition data and documentation:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Each source entry includes a "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Source Type"/><Run Text=" dropdown ("/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Drop"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Shop"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Quest"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Crafting"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Starting"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Event"/><Run Text=") and an optional "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Source Detail"/><Run Text=" text field for notes (e.g., which NPC drops it, which shop sells it)."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Sources can also be auto-populated by the project: when you assign an item to a spawn, loot table, or shop, The Forge can optionally add that assignment as a source entry on the item."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Use the "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Add Source"/><Run Text=" and "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Remove"/><Run Text=" (X) buttons to manage source entries."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Source changes mark the project as dirty and support undo/redo."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Crafting Components -->
            <TextBlock Text="Crafting Components" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="If the item can be crafted, the Crafting Components section defines the required ingredients:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Each component row has a "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Component"/><Run Text=" dropdown that lists all other items defined in the Item Editor. Select the ingredient item from the dropdown."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Quantity"/><Run Text=" &#8212; How many of the component are needed (integer, minimum 1)."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Consumed"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A checkbox indicating whether the component is consumed during crafting or remains (e.g., a mold is not consumed; ingredients are)."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Use the "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Add Component"/><Run Text=" and "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Remove"/><Run Text=" (X) buttons to manage the component list."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; The component dropdown shows all items by Key. Selecting a component item creates a reference link &#8212; if that item is later deleted, validation flags the dangling reference."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Crafting component changes are "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="undoable"/><Run Text=" and mark the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>
            <!-- Metadata: Aliases -->
            <TextBlock Text="Metadata &#8212; Aliases" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="The Metadata section groups several Evennia-compatible attributes. "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Aliases"/><Run Text=" are alternate names players can use to refer to the item:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Enter a "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="comma-separated list"/><Run Text=" of alternate names (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="sword, blade, iron"/><Run Text=" for an Iron Sword)."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Aliases are exported to Evennia as the item's aliases list, allowing players to interact with the item using any of its alternate names."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; The field is a free-text input. Changing aliases marks the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Metadata: Tags -->
            <TextBlock Text="Metadata &#8212; Tags" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Tags are Evennia tags attached to the item, used for categorization, filtering, and gameplay logic:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Enter tags as a "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="comma-separated list"/><Run Text=" (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="weapon, metal, loot"/><Run Text=")."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Tags are exported to Evennia where they can be used in scripts, quests, and dialogue conditions (e.g., checking if a player has an item tagged "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="quest"/><Run Text=")."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; The Tags field is free-text. Changing tags marks the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Metadata: Attributes -->
            <TextBlock Text="Metadata &#8212; Attributes" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Attributes are key-value pairs exported as Evennia attributes on the item. They store structured data used by game systems:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Each attribute row has a "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Key"/><Run Text=" field (the attribute name) and a "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Value"/><Run Text=" field (the data &#8212; string, number, or JSON)."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Examples: "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="weight = 5.2"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="rarity = epic"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="damage_type = fire"/><Run Text="."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Use the "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Add Attribute"/><Run Text=" and "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Remove"/><Run Text=" (X) buttons to manage the attribute list."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Duplicate keys are not allowed"/><Run Text=" &#8212; if you enter the same key twice, the editor shows a validation warning immediately and prevents committing the duplicate until it is resolved."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Attribute changes are undoable and mark the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>
            <!-- Metadata: Permissions -->
            <TextBlock Text="Metadata &#8212; Permissions" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Permissions control who can interact with the item in-game using Evennia's lock system:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Lock String"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A free-text Evennia lock string (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="get:perm(Player);drop:perm(Player)"/><Run Text="). This defines who can pick up, drop, use, or otherwise interact with the item."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Home"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The home location (room key or #dbref) where the item returns if dropped or reset. Leave empty for no home."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Permissions are exported directly to Evennia. The Lock String field is free-text and is not validated by The Forge for syntax correctness &#8212; Evennia will report any lock errors at runtime."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Changing the Lock String or Home marks the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Dirty Tracking -->
            <TextBlock Text="Dirty Tracking" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="The Item Editor integrates with The Forge's project-wide dirty tracking system to ensure you never lose unsaved work:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Any change made in the Item Editor &#8212; creating, deleting, duplicating, or modifying any field of any item &#8212; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="marks the project as dirty"/><Run Text=" (unsaved changes)."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; The dirty state is indicated by an "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="asterisk (*)"/><Run Text=" in the main window title bar (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="MyProject.json *"/><Run Text=")."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Changes are persisted to the project's in-memory data immediately, but are only written to disk when you "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Save"/><Run Text=" (Ctrl+S)."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Closing the Item Editor does not save changes to disk &#8212; only saving the project does. If you close the project or exit The Forge with unsaved changes, you are prompted to save."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Undo/redo operations in the Item Editor also respect dirty tracking: undoing the last change that made the project dirty clears the dirty flag if that was the only unsaved change."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Validation -->
            <TextBlock Text="Item Editor Validation" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="The Forge's validation system checks items for issues that would cause problems during export or in-game. Run validation from the toolbar or menu at any time:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="Item validation rules:"/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="EI001 &#8212; Empty item ID (ERROR)"/><Run Text=": An item has no identifier. This usually indicates data corruption."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="EI002 &#8212; Duplicate item ID (ERROR)"/><Run Text=": Two items share the same ID. Each item must have a unique identifier."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="EI003 &#8212; Duplicate item Key (ERROR)"/><Run Text=": Two items have the same Key. Item keys must be unique across the project."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="EI004 &#8212; Empty item Key (WARNING)"/><Run Text=": An item has no Key set. Items without keys are still exported but will be harder for players and builders to identify."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="DR005 &#8212; Spawn references missing item (ERROR)"/><Run Text=": An item spawn's EntityId points to an item that no longer exists. This occurs when a spawn references an item that has been deleted from the Item Editor. The spawn dropdown will show "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="(none)"/><Run Text=" for the broken reference."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="DR010 &#8212; Crafting component references missing item (ERROR)"/><Run Text=": A crafting component references an item that has been deleted."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="DR011 &#8212; Loot table / shop references missing item (ERROR)"/><Run Text=": A loot table entry or shop inventory slot references an item that no longer exists."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="Validation errors block Evennia export &#8212; you must resolve all errors before exporting your project. Warnings do not block export but should be reviewed."/>
            </TextBlock>
<!-- ============================================ -->
            <!-- NPC Editor Section                              -->
            <!-- ============================================ -->

            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0,20,0,10">
                <Border Background="#4CAF50" Width="4" CornerRadius="1"
                        VerticalAlignment="Stretch" Margin="0,0,10,0"/>
                <TextBlock Text="NPC Editor" FontSize="14" FontWeight="SemiBold"
                           Foreground="#D0D0D0"/>
            </StackPanel>

            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="The "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="NPC Editor"/><Run Text=" is where you define every non-player character (NPC) in your project — monsters, quest givers, merchants, and any other character players can encounter. NPCs created here appear as selectable options in the Monster / NPC Spawns dropdown, in Loot Tables, in Shop inventories, and in Dialogue assignments. The NPC Editor is accessed from the main window."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Opening the NPC Editor -->
            <TextBlock Text="Opening the NPC Editor" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="You can open the NPC Editor in several ways:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Menu bar"/><Run Text=" &#8212; Click "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Tools &#8594; NPC Editor"/><Run Text=" in the main window menu. A separate dialog window opens showing all NPCs currently defined in the project."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Toolbar button"/><Run Text=" &#8212; If the NPC Editor button is present on the toolbar, clicking it opens the editor directly."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Keyboard shortcut"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The NPC Editor has an assigned keyboard shortcut for quick access."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="The NPC Editor opens as a modeless dialog, meaning you can interact with the main map window while the editor remains open. This allows you to reference rooms, spawns, loot tables, shops, and dialogue trees as you work on NPCs."/>
            </TextBlock>
<!-- Creating NPCs -->
            <TextBlock Text="Creating NPCs" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="To add a new NPC to your project:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Click the New NPC button"/><Run Text=" in the NPC Editor toolbar. A new NPC is created with a unique auto-generated ID (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="myproject_npc_0001"/><Run Text=") and default placeholder values."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; The new NPC appears in the list on the left side of the editor and is automatically selected, ready for editing."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Default values for a new NPC include: Key = "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="New NPC"/><Run Text=", Classification = "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Creature"/><Run Text=", Behavior = "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Neutral"/><Run Text=", and empty Description, Notes, Stats, and other fields."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Creating an NPC is a fully "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="undoable"/><Run Text=" operation (Ctrl+Z). Undoing NPC creation removes the NPC from the project and from any spawns, loot tables, shops, or dialogue references that pointed to it."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Selecting NPCs -->
            <TextBlock Text="Selecting NPCs" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="The NPC Editor displays a list of all NPCs on the left side of the dialog:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Click an NPC in the list"/><Run Text=" to select it. The right-side property panel updates to show that NPC's fields for editing."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Search/Filter"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A search box at the top of the NPC list lets you filter by Key (name) or ID to quickly find a specific NPC."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; The selected NPC is highlighted in the list. Only one NPC can be selected at a time."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; If you have unsaved changes in the currently selected NPC's fields, switching to another NPC saves those changes to the project data automatically (and marks the project dirty)."/>
            </TextBlock>
<!-- Duplicating NPCs -->
            <TextBlock Text="Duplicating NPCs" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="You can create a copy of an existing NPC to use as a starting point for a new one:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Select the NPC"/><Run Text=" you want to duplicate in the list."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Click the "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Duplicate"/><Run Text=" button. A new NPC is created with a unique ID and the same Key appended with "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text=" (Copy)"/><Run Text="."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="All properties are copied"/><Run Text=" &#8212; Stats, Combat Settings, Classification, Behavior, Abilities, Resistances, Equipment, Inventory, Patrol Waypoints, Loot Table assignment, Dialogue assignment, and all Metadata fields (Aliases, Tags, Attributes, Permissions) are duplicated exactly."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; The duplicated NPC is automatically selected and scrolled into view in the list."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Duplication is an "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="undoable"/><Run Text=" operation (Ctrl+Z)."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Deleting NPCs -->
            <TextBlock Text="Deleting NPCs" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="To permanently remove an NPC from the project:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Select the NPC"/><Run Text=" in the list and click the "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Delete"/><Run Text=" button."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; A "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="confirmation dialog"/><Run Text=" appears, warning you that deleting this NPC will also affect any spawns, loot tables, shops, or dialogue references that reference it. The dialog lists the number of references that will be broken."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; If you confirm, the NPC is removed from the project and any references to it (in spawns, shops, loot tables, dialogue, etc.) are set to "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="(none)"/><Run Text=" &#8212; becoming dangling references that validation will flag."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Deletion is an "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="undoable"/><Run Text=" operation (Ctrl+Z). Undoing restores the NPC and re-links any references that were broken."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- ID, Key, and Name Fields -->
            <TextBlock Text="NPC ID, Key, and Name" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Every NPC has three fundamental identifier fields:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="ID"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A read-only unique identifier auto-generated when the NPC is created (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="myproject_npc_0001"/><Run Text="). The ID is used internally to link NPCs to spawns, loot tables, shops, dialogue trees, and quests. It cannot be changed after creation to preserve referential integrity."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Key"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The primary display name of the NPC (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Goblin Warrior"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Elder Mage"/><Run Text="). This is what players see in-game and what appears in spawn dropdowns, shop keeper lists, and dialogue assignments. The Key must be unique across all NPCs &#8212; the editor validates this and shows an error if you enter a duplicate Key."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Name"/><Run Text=" &#8212; An optional display name that can differ from the Key. When set, the Name field overrides the Key for in-game display purposes. This is useful for NPCs that have a short Key for reference but a longer, more descriptive Name for players (e.g., Key = "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="goblin_scout"/><Run Text=", Name = "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Scout of the Crimson Fang Tribe"/><Run Text=")."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Changing the Key or Name marks the project as dirty. If you change the Key to a value already used by another NPC, a validation message appears immediately, and the change is not committed until the conflict is resolved."/>
            </TextBlock>
<!-- Description and Notes -->
            <TextBlock Text="Description and Notes" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Every NPC has two text areas for documentation and in-game flavor:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Description"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The in-game description shown to players when they look at or examine the NPC. This is the narrative flavor text that brings the NPC to life (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="A short, wiry goblin clad in scavenged leather armor. Its beady eyes dart nervously."/><Run Text=")."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Notes"/><Run Text=" &#8212; Internal builder notes not shown to players. Use this field for documentation, design intent, quest hooks, or reminders for yourself and your team. Notes are for editor reference only and are not exported to Evennia."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Both fields are free-text multi-line text areas. Changing either field marks the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Stats -->
            <TextBlock Text="Stats" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="The Stats section defines the NPC's core numerical attributes used in combat and gameplay calculations:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="HP (Hit Points)"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The NPC's maximum health. Determines how much damage the NPC can withstand before being defeated."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="MP (Mana Points)"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The NPC's magical energy pool, consumed when casting spells or using special abilities."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Attack"/><Run Text=" &#8212; Base physical damage dealt per hit before modifiers. Higher values make the NPC more dangerous in melee combat."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Defense"/><Run Text=" &#8212; Damage reduction applied to incoming physical attacks. Higher values make the NPC harder to damage."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Speed"/><Run Text=" &#8212; Determines turn order in combat. NPCs with higher Speed act before slower characters."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Level"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The NPC's relative power tier. Level is used for XP reward calculations and difficulty scaling."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Each stat is a numeric field. Entering non-numeric values is rejected immediately. All stat changes are "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="undoable"/><Run Text=" and mark the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>
<!-- Combat Settings -->
            <TextBlock Text="Combat Settings" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Combat Settings control how the NPC behaves during encounters:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Aggression Range"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The distance (in room units or grid cells) at which the NPC will detect and engage players. Set to 0 for passive NPCs that never initiate combat."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Flee Threshold"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The HP percentage at which the NPC will attempt to flee combat. For example, a value of 25 means the NPC flees when its HP drops to 25% or below. Set to 0 to disable fleeing."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Combat Style"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A dropdown defining the NPC's combat role: "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Melee"/><Run Text=" (close-range fighter), "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Ranged"/><Run Text=" (attacks from a distance), "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Caster"/><Run Text=" (prioritizes spells and abilities), "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Healer"/><Run Text=" (supports allies), or "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Mixed"/><Run Text=" (adapts to the situation)."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="XP Reward"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The amount of experience points awarded to players who defeat this NPC. Set to 0 for non-combat NPCs."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; All combat settings are numeric or dropdown fields. Changes are undoable and mark the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Classification -->
            <TextBlock Text="Classification" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Classification defines the NPC's type and faction, affecting how other NPCs and game systems interact with them:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="NPC Type"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A dropdown categorizing the NPC's nature: "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Creature"/><Run Text=" (monsters, animals, beasts), "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Humanoid"/><Run Text=" (people, races), "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Undead"/><Run Text=" (skeletons, zombies, ghosts), "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Construct"/><Run Text=" (golems, automatons), "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Elemental"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Dragon"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Demon"/><Run Text=", and "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Boss"/><Run Text="."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Faction"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The NPC's allegiance group (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Hostile"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Friendly"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Neutral"/><Run Text=", or custom factions like "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Goblin Horde"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Town Guard"/><Run Text="). NPCs of the same faction do not attack each other."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Is Unique"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A checkbox indicating whether this NPC is a one-of-a-kind character (e.g., a named quest boss) or a generic spawnable creature. Unique NPCs are flagged in export so Evennia can enforce single-instance spawning."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Type and Faction are dropdown selections. Changing classification marks the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>
<!-- Behavior -->
            <TextBlock Text="Behavior" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Behavior controls the NPC's default stance and idle routines outside of combat:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Default Stance"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A dropdown defining how the NPC reacts to players when not in combat: "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Neutral"/><Run Text=" (ignores players unless provoked), "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Friendly"/><Run Text=" (welcomes players, may offer help), "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Hostile"/><Run Text=" (attacks on sight), "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Fearful"/><Run Text=" (flees from players), or "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Guard"/><Run Text=" (stands watch, attacks intruders in a defined area)."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Idle Behavior"/><Run Text=" &#8212; What the NPC does when not interacting with players: "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Stand Still"/><Run Text=" (stays in place), "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Wander"/><Run Text=" (roams randomly within the room or patrol area), "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Follow Path"/><Run Text=" (walks a fixed patrol route defined by waypoints), or "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Scripted"/><Run Text=" (runs custom behavior scripts)."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Talkative"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A checkbox indicating whether the NPC can be spoken to. Talkative NPCs can have dialogue assigned. Non-talkative NPCs are purely combat or environmental."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Behavior settings are dropdowns and checkboxes. Changing behavior marks the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>
<!-- Abilities -->
            <TextBlock Text="Abilities" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Abilities define special actions the NPC can perform in combat or in the world. Each ability entry has several fields:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Name"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The display name of the ability (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Fire Breath"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Backstab"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Healing Wave"/><Run Text=")."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Type"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The category of ability: "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Physical"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Magical"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Status"/><Run Text=" (buffs/debuffs), "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Heal"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Summon"/><Run Text=", or "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Script"/><Run Text=" (custom behavior)."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Power"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A numeric value indicating the ability's strength. Higher values mean more damage, stronger heals, or more potent effects."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="MP Cost"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The mana points required to use this ability. The NPC must have sufficient remaining MP to execute the ability."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Cooldown"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The number of combat rounds the NPC must wait before using this ability again. Set to 0 for abilities that can be used every round."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Target"/><Run Text=" &#8212; Who the ability affects: "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Single Enemy"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="All Enemies"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Self"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Single Ally"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="All Allies"/><Run Text=", or "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Area"/><Run Text="."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Use the "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Add Ability"/><Run Text=" button to create a new ability row. Use the "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Remove"/><Run Text=" button (X) on each row to delete that ability."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Ability changes (add, remove, edit) are all "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="undoable"/><Run Text=" and mark the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>
<!-- Resistances -->
            <TextBlock Text="Resistances" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Resistances define the NPC's vulnerability or immunity to different damage types and status effects. Each resistance entry has two components:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Type"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The damage type or effect being resisted: "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Physical"/><Run Text=" (slashing, piercing, bludgeoning), "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Fire"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Ice"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Lightning"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Poison"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Holy"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Dark"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Arcane"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Stun"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Sleep"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Fear"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Charm"/><Run Text=", or other custom types."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Value"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A percentage indicating the resistance level: "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="100"/><Run Text=" = full immunity, "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="50"/><Run Text=" = half damage/effect duration, "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="0"/><Run Text=" = normal damage, "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="-50"/><Run Text=" = 50% extra weakness (takes bonus damage)."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; For example, a Fire Elemental might have "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Fire = 100"/><Run Text=" (immune) and "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Ice = -50"/><Run Text=" (weak). A Skeleton might have "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Piercing = 50"/><Run Text=" (resistant) and "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Holy = -25"/><Run Text=" (weak)."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Use the "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Add Resistance"/><Run Text=" and "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Remove"/><Run Text=" (X) buttons to manage the resistance list."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Resistance changes are undoable and mark the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Equipment -->
            <TextBlock Text="Equipment" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Equipment defines the items the NPC has actively equipped — its weapon, armor, and accessories. These items affect the NPC's combat stats and are dropped on defeat if configured:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Weapon"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A dropdown selector referencing an item from the Item Editor. The equipped weapon contributes its Attack modifier to the NPC's combat stats."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Armor"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A dropdown referencing an armor item. The armor's Defense modifier is added to the NPC's base Defense."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Accessory"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A dropdown referencing an accessory or trinket item. Accessories may provide special modifiers, resistances, or effects."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Shield"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A dropdown referencing a shield item. Contributes additional Defense and may enable blocking mechanics."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Each equipment slot is optional — leave any slot empty if the NPC does not use that equipment type."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; The dropdown shows all items currently defined in the Item Editor. If the referenced item is deleted from the Item Editor, the slot shows "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="(none)"/><Run Text=" and a validation warning (DR012) will be raised."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Equipment changes mark the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>
<!-- Inventory -->
            <TextBlock Text="Inventory" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Inventory defines items the NPC carries that are not actively equipped but may be dropped as loot upon defeat. This is distinct from the Loot Table assignment — inventory items are guaranteed drops, while loot table items are rolled randomly:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Each inventory entry has an "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Item"/><Run Text=" dropdown (referencing an item from the Item Editor) and a "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Quantity"/><Run Text=" field."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Drop Chance"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A percentage (0-100) controlling whether the item drops on defeat. Set to 100 for guaranteed drops, lower values for random chance."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Use the "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Add Inventory Item"/><Run Text=" and "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Remove"/><Run Text=" (X) buttons to manage the inventory list."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Inventory items are separate from the Loot Table assignment — the Loot Table provides randomized rewards, while Inventory represents specific items the NPC is known to carry."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Inventory changes (add, remove, edit) are all "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="undoable"/><Run Text=" and mark the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>
<!-- Patrol Waypoints -->
            <TextBlock Text="Patrol Waypoints" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Patrol Waypoints define a fixed route the NPC follows when its Idle Behavior is set to "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="Follow Path"/><Run Text=". Waypoints are a sequence of room or location identifiers:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Each waypoint entry specifies a "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Room ID"/><Run Text=" &#8212; the destination room the NPC moves to. Rooms are selected from a dropdown showing all rooms in the current project."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Wait Time"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The number of seconds the NPC pauses at this waypoint before moving to the next one. Set to 0 for continuous movement."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; The NPC follows waypoints in order from top to bottom. Upon reaching the last waypoint, the NPC either "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Loops"/><Run Text=" (returns to the first waypoint) or "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Reverses"/><Run Text=" (walks back through the waypoints in reverse), depending on the Loop/Reverse toggle."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Use the "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Add Waypoint"/><Run Text=" and "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Remove"/><Run Text=" (X) buttons to manage the patrol path. Use the "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Move Up"/><Run Text=" and "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Move Down"/><Run Text=" arrows to reorder waypoints."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Waypoint changes are "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="undoable"/><Run Text=" and mark the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Loot Table Assignment -->
            <TextBlock Text="Loot Table Assignment" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="The Loot Table assignment connects an NPC to a randomized loot drop system. This is separate from the NPC's Inventory (guaranteed drops):"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Loot Table"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A dropdown selector listing all loot tables defined in the Loot Table Editor. Selecting a loot table means that when the NPC is defeated, the game rolls on that table to determine random drops."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; An NPC can be assigned to "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="at most one"/><Run Text=" loot table at a time. The dropdown selection is single-choice."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="None"/><Run Text=" is a valid selection — leave it at None if the NPC should not drop random loot (it may still drop Inventory items if configured)."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; If the assigned loot table is deleted from the Loot Table Editor, the dropdown reverts to "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="(none)"/><Run Text=" and a validation warning is raised."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Changing the loot table assignment marks the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Dialogue Assignment -->
            <TextBlock Text="Dialogue Assignment" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="The Dialogue assignment connects an NPC to a conversation tree defined in the Dialogue Editor. This is what players interact with when they speak to the NPC:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Dialogue"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A dropdown selector listing all dialogue trees defined in the Dialogue Editor. Selecting a dialogue tree makes it the NPC's conversation script when a player initiates dialogue."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Only NPCs with "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Talkative"/><Run Text=" checked in the Behavior section can have dialogue assigned. The dialogue dropdown is disabled for non-talkative NPCs."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; An NPC can be assigned to "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="at most one"/><Run Text=" dialogue tree. "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="(none)"/><Run Text=" means the NPC has no conversation (players will see a generic message when attempting to talk)."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; If the assigned dialogue tree is deleted from the Dialogue Editor, the dropdown reverts to "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="(none)"/><Run Text=" and a validation warning is raised."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Changing the dialogue assignment marks the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>
<!-- Metadata: Aliases -->
            <TextBlock Text="Metadata &#8212; Aliases" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Aliases are alternate names or keywords that players can use to refer to the NPC:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Enter a "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="comma-separated list"/><Run Text=" of alternate names (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="goblin, scout, greenskin"/><Run Text=")."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Aliases are exported to Evennia, allowing players to target or refer to the NPC by any of these names."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; The Aliases field is free-text. Changing aliases marks the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Metadata: Tags -->
            <TextBlock Text="Metadata &#8212; Tags" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Tags are labels applied to the NPC for categorization, quest scripting, and game logic:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Enter a "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="comma-separated list"/><Run Text=" (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="monster, goblin, quest, elite"/><Run Text=")."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Tags are exported to Evennia where they can be used in scripts, quests, and dialogue conditions (e.g., checking if an NPC is tagged "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="boss"/><Run Text=" or "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="undead"/><Run Text=")."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; The Tags field is free-text. Changing tags marks the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Metadata: Attributes -->
            <TextBlock Text="Metadata &#8212; Attributes" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Attributes are key-value pairs exported as Evennia attributes on the NPC. They store structured data used by game systems:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Each attribute row has a "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Key"/><Run Text=" field (the attribute name) and a "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Value"/><Run Text=" field (the data &#8212; string, number, or JSON)."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Examples: "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="faction_rank = lieutenant"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="quest_giver = true"/><Run Text=", "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="spawn_limit = 3"/><Run Text="."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Use the "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Add Attribute"/><Run Text=" and "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Remove"/><Run Text=" (X) buttons to manage the attribute list."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Duplicate keys are not allowed"/><Run Text=" &#8212; if you enter the same key twice, the editor shows a validation warning immediately and prevents committing the duplicate until it is resolved."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Attribute changes are undoable and mark the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Metadata: Permissions -->
            <TextBlock Text="Metadata &#8212; Permissions" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="Permissions control who can interact with the NPC in-game using Evennia's lock system:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Lock String"/><Run Text=" &#8212; A free-text Evennia lock string (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="control:perm(Builder);delete:perm(Admin)"/><Run Text="). This defines who can manage, control, or otherwise interact with the NPC as an admin or builder."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Home"/><Run Text=" &#8212; The home location (room key or #dbref) where the NPC returns if reset or after a server restart. Leave empty for no home location."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Permissions are exported directly to Evennia. The Lock String field is free-text and is not validated by The Forge for syntax correctness &#8212; Evennia will report any lock errors at runtime."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Changing the Lock String or Home marks the project as dirty."/>
            </TextBlock>
<!-- Dirty Tracking -->
            <TextBlock Text="Dirty Tracking" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="The NPC Editor integrates with The Forge's project-wide dirty tracking system to ensure you never lose unsaved work:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Any change made in the NPC Editor &#8212; creating, deleting, duplicating, or modifying any field of any NPC &#8212; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="marks the project as dirty"/><Run Text=" (unsaved changes)."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; The dirty state is indicated by an "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="asterisk (*)"/><Run Text=" in the main window title bar (e.g., "/><Run FontStyle="Italic" Text="MyProject.json *"/><Run Text=")."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Changes are persisted to the project's in-memory data immediately, but are only written to disk when you "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="Save"/><Run Text=" (Ctrl+S)."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Closing the NPC Editor does not save changes to disk &#8212; only saving the project does. If you close the project or exit The Forge with unsaved changes, you are prompted to save."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; Undo/redo operations in the NPC Editor also respect dirty tracking: undoing the last change that made the project dirty clears the dirty flag if that was the only unsaved change."/>
            </TextBlock>

            <!-- Validation -->
            <TextBlock Text="NPC Editor Validation" FontSize="13"
                       FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#B0B0B0" Margin="8,12,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock FontSize="12" Foreground="#808080" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                <Run Text="The Forge's validation system checks NPCs for issues that would cause problems during export or in-game. Run validation from the toolbar or menu at any time:"/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="NPC validation rules:"/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="EN001 &#8212; Empty NPC ID (ERROR)"/><Run Text=": An NPC has no identifier. This usually indicates data corruption."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="EN002 &#8212; Duplicate NPC ID (ERROR)"/><Run Text=": Two NPCs share the same ID. Each NPC must have a unique identifier."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="EN003 &#8212; Duplicate NPC Key (ERROR)"/><Run Text=": Two NPCs have the same Key. NPC keys must be unique across the project."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="EN004 &#8212; Empty NPC Key (WARNING)"/><Run Text=": An NPC has no Key set. NPCs without keys are still exported but will be harder for players and builders to identify."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="DR012 &#8212; NPC spawn references missing NPC (ERROR)"/><Run Text=": An NPC spawn's EntityId points to an NPC that no longer exists. This occurs when a spawn references an NPC that has been deleted from the NPC Editor."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="DR013 &#8212; Loot table / shop references missing NPC (ERROR)"/><Run Text=": A loot table entry or shop inventory slot references an NPC that no longer exists."/>
                <LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="&#8226; "/><Run FontWeight="SemiBold" Text="DR014 &#8212; Dialogue references missing NPC (ERROR)"/><Run Text=": A dialogue assignment or trigger references an NPC that has been deleted."/>
                <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
                <Run Text="Validation errors block Evennia export &#8212; you must resolve all errors before exporting your project. Warnings do not block export but should be reviewed."/>
            </TextBlock>
            <!-- Close button -->
            <Button Content="Close" Width="80" Height="28" Margin="0,20,0,0"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                    Background="#3E3E42" Foreground="#CCC"
                    BorderBrush="Transparent"
                    Click="Close_Click" IsCancel="True"/>
        </StackPanel>
    </ScrollViewer>
</Window>